      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the posed fixture sweep reads a band as a flat-ended cylinder\n\nThe posed sweep of fixture laws (c2)/(d2) placed each band of a leaning\nstack as a capsule, whose caps reach a whole band radius past each end:\na holder standing 0.5 mm over a clamp was convicted at any lean. A box\nthe capsule reaches is now read a second time against the band as the\ncylinder it is - the interval's tip chord swept exactly, the cylinder\nabout the midpoint pose, a ball for the swing and the arc bulge (the\nfixture mesh law's enclosure) - and cleared only on a GJK proof of a\nseparating plane. The rim reaches R sin θ past the end plane, so the\nverdict turns at the lean where the true band touches.\n\nBoth enclosures contain the swept band, so the law stays conservative;\nnon-finite input or an unfinished search is never a proof.\n\nFixes #1305\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
